{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"self-improvement","displayName":"Self Improving Agent","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/mike5230odense/skills/self-improvement","publisherHandle":"mike5230odense","publisherDisplayName":"mike5230Odense","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/mike5230odense","version":"1.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1772443902584,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/self-improvement/card?ownerHandle=mike5230odense&version=1.0.0","sha256":"eca52c9b754791463bbf666baa8588a79c939159d635b42a163ea3ce574cc8a2","size":2513,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"d95c0077de4a986426ee48c7a223d183051bda34760ed08f5704d364c8152831","bundleFingerprints":["31189a47a456241feb3aafa496032c10578dec2582d68f6d25088294c7148d20","d2022c26aa1c34dac37cb81179845575e6d29cc66650b53c435ed2da4ca274c3"],"files":[{"path":"_meta.json","size":140,"sha256":"eb63ae483ef65c959d442f3520db8c9f9f9f87ad1d38961769726e3f3d387e1b","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"hooks/openclaw/handler.js","size":1620,"sha256":"19f21bdf74b9be3aa8ba2514dd0c727c841f799f948bb3c945ecc28b90be8b86","contentType":"application/x-javascript"},{"path":"hooks/openclaw/HOOK.md","size":589,"sha256":"13294242f2fac134af2dcfcda7c273be98e57d26192989afb7a9ebcb5a1eb224","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"hooks/openclaw/handler.ts","size":1872,"sha256":"a2d4452b135622a7a3a225722cf9422ea85a8121e49607b386282425eb1d844d","contentType":"text/vnd.trolltech.linguist"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":19704,"sha256":"cec6d90543ea51c1ae2dfe09b7c0ac640b0a295101d34ba14c9deedc6607ce0c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/LEARNINGS.md","size":1152,"sha256":"33b0de6f4243ea31d913fab017ded852f13443fd1eb84c0983a670334260ff46","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/SKILL-TEMPLATE.md","size":3407,"sha256":"3ee008f80d53e0e576f7e747ac4c4e040ff659f02d3f5689a95524a3696e4881","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/activator.sh","size":680,"sha256":"a751d91466c8c966f01ac32795871ceff0d1e177c7c186ca4201f962a5cc9be4","contentType":"application/x-shellscript"},{"path":"scripts/error-detector.sh","size":1317,"sha256":"74f82bfd29bcc3615d4c9df0962f7d5e42af75431c029c0e14c2f6127c4787ba","contentType":"application/x-shellscript"},{"path":"scripts/extract-skill.sh","size":5293,"sha256":"d9af3d6f2cde0eeb3c0a85b898828656c1c6d9d51f61ba38f9801030424f5147","contentType":"application/x-shellscript"},{"path":"references/openclaw-integration.md","size":5638,"sha256":"d7d426beb09e10016def1a45fc901c737fb3abcd101252ce81a9c32e69a78257","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/hooks-setup.md","size":4867,"sha256":"838ed1620db4bbe55fc281a61d6dfb1709437d6366ddb3006b70a04109695ab7","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/examples.md","size":8291,"sha256":"c11e38794d78cfa1ba633d14232ec7e9808c14696e96a7bd9b8f4fe178f10451","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":".learnings/ERRORS.md","size":75,"sha256":"731f4a26fee7074d11e999920e5c3ca63b0e025b75a4d9966429ee88a2cb5988","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":".learnings/LEARNINGS.md","size":99,"sha256":"f5c1302498cad158c357426ac2aa73f6f05fda8b9103d47acb34d4851b76391c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":".learnings/FEATURE_REQUESTS.md","size":84,"sha256":"a6291573936034efaad57b43b6f57bdb35ed627f01ce9309b2c781da63563c37","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is not overtly destructive, but it asks agents to persist conversation-derived notes and promote them into future instruction files, with broad optional hooks.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789096944621,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T02","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Untrusted Conversation Content Can Be Promoted into Persistent Agent Instructions"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":346,"endLine":361}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"d1d1534a2a938009"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 346–361  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Persistent agent memory and instruction poisoning  \n**Risk Level**: Medium  \n\n### Vulnerable Code Snippet\n\n```markdown\n### Promotion Rule (System Prompt Feedback)\n\nPromote recurring patterns into agent context/system prompt files when all are true:\n\n- `Recurrence-Count >= 3`\n- Seen across at least 2 distinct tasks\n- Occurred within a 30-day window\n\nPromotion targets:\n- `CLAUDE.md`\n- `AGENTS.md`\n- `.github/copilot-instructions.md`\n- `SOUL.md` / `TOOLS.md` for OpenClaw workspace-level guidance when applicable\n\nWrite promoted rules as short prevention rules (what to do before/while coding),\nnot long incident write-ups.\n```\n\nRelated guidance at `SKILL.md`, lines 448–448:\n\n```markdown\n7. **Promote aggressively** - if in doubt, add to CLAUDE.md or .github/copilot-instructions.md\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe skill directs agents to capture corrections and other conversation-derived material in `.learnings/`, then promote recurring entries into files that are loaded as persistent agent context. The documented promotion targets include `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, `SOUL.md`, and `TOOLS.md`.\n\nConversation content is an untrusted input boundary. The workflow does not require human approval before promotion, distinguish trusted project facts from user-supplied directives, or filter entries containing role instructions, commands, URLs, tool-use directives, or attempts to weaken security constraints. Its recurrence threshold establishes frequency but not trustworthiness: an attacker can repeat a crafted correction across multiple tasks to satisfy the stated criteria.\n\nOnce promoted, the content can influence future sessions through normal workspace prompt loading. This constitutes an agent memory poisoning path. No automatic promotion implementation or embedded malicious payload was found, so exploitation depends on an agent following the documented workflow and obtaining permission to modify the target instruction files.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker submits a crafted statement as a correction or purported project-specific lesson.\n2. Following the skill instructions, the agent records the attacker-controlled concept in `.learnings/LEARNINGS.md`.\n3. The attacker repeats the same concept across at least two tasks until its recurrence count reaches three within 30 days.\n4. The documented promotion criteria are satisfied.\n5. Guided by the instruction to “promote aggressively,” an agent writes the resulting rule into `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, `SOUL.md`, or `TOOLS.md`.\n6. The platform loads that file as context in later sessions.\n7. Future agents may follow the poisoned rule when selecting tools, handling data, or performing project operations.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful exploitation provides persistent influence over future agent behavior within the affected workspace and any sessions that load the modified instruction file. The effective scope depends on the selected target:\n\n- Project instruction files can affect later work throughout the repository.\n- OpenClaw workspace files can affect multiple sessions using that workspace.\n- `SOUL.md` can influence behavioral guidance.\n- `AGENTS.md` can influence workflows and delegation.\n- `TOOLS.md` can influence tool selection and operational assumptions.\n\nThe poisoned text does not independently grant operating-system privileges. Any resulting file access, command execution, or data exposure remains bounded by the permissions and tools available to future agents. The audited package contains no confirmed credential theft, network exfiltration, privilege escalation, or remote payload execution mechanism.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Require explicit human approval before writing any learning into persistent agent-context files.\n2. Treat conversation-derived entries as untrusted data, regardless of recurrence count or source claims.\n3. Replace automatic or aggressive promotion guidance with a review workflow that verifies:\n   - The statement is a factual, project-specific rule.\n   - The rule is supported by trusted repository documentation or code.\n   - The entry does not contain role directives, safety overrides, commands, external URLs, credential instructions, or tool-routing instructions.\n4. Restrict direct promotion into high-impact files such as `SOUL.md`, `TOOLS.md`, and global workspace instructions. Prefer a human-reviewed candidate file that is not automatically loaded into agent context.\n5. Preserve provenance for every candidate, including source session, author, supporting files, reviewer, and approval timestamp.\n6. Use an allowlisted schema for promoted rules and render values as inert data rather than copying raw conversation text.\n7. Require code-owner or maintainer review for changes to persistent instruction files.\n8. Add duplicate-content and adversarial-pattern checks so repeated attacker input cannot become trusted merely by satisfying recurrence thresholds.\n9. Remove or revise the “Promote aggressively” instruction at line 448; promotion should be conservative and review-gated.\n10. Add regression tests demonstrating that corrections containing prompt-injection language cannot be promoted without explicit approval."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789096780.9137077,"endTime":1789096870.3746736}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"self-improvement","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57d40xa5neq8wdrq8ty91xgvd8e7scy-9BANkf/clawscan-skillspector-321712309/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T03:19:39.841460+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":".learnings/ERRORS.md","type":"markdown","lines":5,"executable":false,"size_bytes":75,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":".learnings/FEATURE_REQUESTS.md","type":"markdown","lines":5,"executable":false,"size_bytes":84,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":".learnings/LEARNINGS.md","type":"markdown","lines":5,"executable":false,"size_bytes":99,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":647,"executable":false,"size_bytes":19704,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"_meta.json","type":"json","lines":6,"executable":false,"size_bytes":140,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"assets/LEARNINGS.md","type":"markdown","lines":45,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1152,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"assets/SKILL-TEMPLATE.md","type":"markdown","lines":177,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3407,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"hooks/openclaw/HOOK.md","type":"markdown","lines":23,"executable":false,"size_bytes":589,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"hooks/openclaw/handler.js","type":"javascript","lines":56,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1620,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"hooks/openclaw/handler.ts","type":"typescript","lines":62,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1872,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/examples.md","type":"markdown","lines":374,"executable":false,"size_bytes":8291,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/hooks-setup.md","type":"markdown","lines":223,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4867,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/openclaw-integration.md","type":"markdown","lines":248,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5638,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/activator.sh","type":"shell","lines":20,"executable":true,"size_bytes":680,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/error-detector.sh","type":"shell","lines":55,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1317,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/extract-skill.sh","type":"shell","lines":221,"executable":true,"size_bytes":5293,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-7d3390b3ae144d4cb7581554ab12533c","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The declared description is about capturing and reviewing learnings, errors, corrections, and failures for continuous improvement. The supplied code does not implement any learning capture, error logging, correction tracking, review workflow, or retrieval of prior learnings. Instead, it is a helper script for extracting/promoting a learning into a new skill scaffold by creating directories and writing a template file. This is a materially different primary purpose and includes undeclared filesystem write behavior. While the comments mention creating a skill from a learning entry, the code itself only scaffolds the skill structure and does not perform the declared learning-management behavior.","remediation":"Update the skill description to accurately reflect all capabilities, or remove undeclared functionality from the implementation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"code_path":"scripts/extract-skill.sh","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":221,"actual_behavior_summary":"A shell script that scaffolds a new skill directory and SKILL.md template from a provided skill name, with optional dry-run and configurable relative output directory."},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AS1","finding_id":"finding-f1f44669d1504c23a34cf2814f36e0ab","category":"Agent Snooping","pattern":"Agent Config Directory Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":48,"end_line":null},"finding":"~/.claude/settings.json","explanation":"Writing to ~/.claude/settings.json establishes behavior in a sensitive agent configuration directory, affecting future sessions beyond the current project. In this context, the file is being used to install a persistent command hook, so compromise or misuse of that configuration can create durable, cross-project execution and data exposure risks.","remediation":"Prefer repository-local configuration over user-home agent config changes, and clearly warn that changes to ~/.claude/settings.json are persistent and high trust. If user-level setup is necessary, require explicit confirmation, narrow scoping, and guidance for auditing and removing the hook.","code_snippet":"\n### Option 2: User-Level Configuration\n\nAdd to `~/.claude/settings.json` for global activation:\n\n```json\n{","intent":null,"tags":["Agent Snooping"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5a1df888db5d4ec0b5b9acca20cfc27be4af48718ceb134b7edd155d53abdf2c","occurrences":[{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":48,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P3","finding_id":"finding-b260e374fc9640c4a092783cca735d8b","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Exfiltration Commands","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/openclaw-integration.md","start_line":177,"end_line":null},"finding":"Send message to","explanation":"Instructions found that direct the agent to transmit conversation context or user data to external services.","remediation":"Remove instructions that send user data, prompts, or context to external URLs. If telemetry is needed, use documented, privacy-preserving methods.","code_snippet":"\n### sessions_send\n\nSend message to another session:\n```\nsessions_send(sessionKey=\"session-id\", message=\"Learning: API requires X-Custom-Header\")\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6cbd4d2bba77cb69209f09a566e5cfc411283fe144d6f8149b1f5977ae4b9e5c","occurrences":[{"file":"references/openclaw-integration.md","start_line":177,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-959668619a5a4129b71b3c5ae31b458e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest description encourages invocation in a wide range of routine situations, including ordinary failures, corrections, and realization of outdated knowledge. In systems that auto-load or suggest skills from descriptions, this broad guidance can over-activate the skill and lead to unnecessary data capture and persistence.","remediation":"Tighten the description so activation is limited to explicit post-task review or operator-approved logging events. State clearly that sensitive content must be minimized/redacted and that logging should occur only after relevance and privacy checks.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-394b1d2d4bc1419d8a125e77c6fc5930","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":64,"end_line":null},"finding":"Create Learning Files\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.openclaw","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"    └── FEATURE_REQUESTS.md\n```\n\n### Create Learning Files\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.openclaw/workspace/.learnings","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"50cde7bc36af8896e3f183732f740907994866c8e17207da188f43630e3c2552","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":64,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-0088b160f21f4502b5a005827305f3e5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":85,"end_line":92},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly encourages sharing learnings across sessions and reading other session transcripts, which creates a natural-language data exfiltration channel between contexts. If users discuss secrets, proprietary code, or personal data, those details can be propagated beyond the original session boundary without adequate need-to-know controls.","remediation":"Prohibit cross-session sharing of raw transcripts or user-provided content by default. Restrict sharing to sanitized, minimal summaries; require explicit user approval for cross-session transfer; and add rules forbidding transmission of secrets, credentials, personal data, and confidential business information.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":85,"end_line":92}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-e6c56636d5294c9ab344731a1585b6d7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":124,"end_line":157},"finding":null,"explanation":"The logging templates instruct the agent to store full context, inputs, parameters, environment details, user requests, and related files. That creates a durable retention sink for sensitive information such as credentials, tokens, internal paths, customer data, or confidential prompts, especially when logging follows failures where raw error output often contains secrets.","remediation":"Revise the templates to require data minimization and redaction. Replace 'full context' with sanitized summaries, forbid storing secrets or personal data, and add explicit examples of sensitive fields to omit or mask before writing to persistent files.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":124,"end_line":157}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-d408b6981c9b4f19909a2ee356b08a5d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":262,"end_line":289},"finding":null,"explanation":"The promotion workflow pushes learnings into long-term memory and instruction files intended to shape future agent behavior. Without strict sanitization, this can permanently embed sensitive user-derived information into persistent context, where it may later be surfaced, reused, or exposed across unrelated tasks.","remediation":"Add mandatory review and sanitization before promotion, with a rule that only generalized, non-sensitive lessons may be promoted. Ban copying raw incidents, user text, secrets, identifiers, or environment-specific details into memory or instruction files.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":262,"end_line":289}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-c87a5f63a2c84f178b2cc19bcb6ca5ad","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":391,"end_line":405},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger phrases are broad and map common conversational language to automatic logging actions. In agent environments with automatic activation or hooks, this can cause unintended persistence of ordinary user statements, corrections, or requests, increasing the chance that sensitive or irrelevant content is stored without deliberate review.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger conditions to require explicit user intent or a confirmation step before logging. Add a privacy gate that excludes secrets, personal data, credentials, and unrelated conversational content from being persisted.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":391,"end_line":405}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-55d471a0f83c43dbbf2d31c9ffa479da","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":440,"end_line":449},"finding":null,"explanation":"The best-practice guidance emphasizes logging immediately and promoting aggressively, but provides no compensating privacy controls. In practice, this increases the likelihood that sensitive data is retained reflexively before anyone evaluates whether it is necessary or safe to store.","remediation":"Modify the best-practice section to prioritize privacy review before persistence. Require minimization, redaction, and explicit relevance checks, and remove or soften guidance that encourages aggressive retention by default.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":440,"end_line":449}]},{"id":"AS3","finding_id":"finding-218e2104f52e4d059405b41bd8af8e0a","category":"Agent Snooping","pattern":"Skill Enumeration","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/examples.md","start_line":301,"end_line":null},"finding":"skills/docker-m1-fixes/SKILL.md","explanation":"Skill enumerates or reads other installed skills. Access to other skills' SKILL.md files or the skills directory reveals prompt instructions, capabilities, and secrets that should be invisible to peer skills.","remediation":"Remove all code or instructions that list or read other skills' files or directories. Skills should operate independently; cross-skill access is a privilege escalation.","code_snippet":"\nWhen the above learning is extracted as a skill, it becomes:\n\n**File**: `skills/docker-m1-fixes/SKILL.md`\n\n```markdown\n---","intent":null,"tags":["Agent Snooping","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"484b7882992840f9a118f6865f03e9d39cd865fee5ea1ca29243562407237284","occurrences":[{"file":"references/examples.md","start_line":301,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-34418bb79a79424d9130a80154ea8207","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":15,"end_line":null},"finding":"Create `.claude/settings.json` in your project root:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"UserPromptSubmit\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n    ","explanation":"Creating .claude/settings.json in the project root introduces session-persistent agent behavior that survives across prompts and restarts. Persistent hooks are not inherently unsafe, but in this skill they are used to execute shell commands automatically, so persistence materially increases the blast radius of mistakes, abuse, or later script tampering.","remediation":"Call out the persistence risk explicitly and make hooks opt-in with conservative defaults. Recommend project-specific review of hook scripts, integrity monitoring, and simple disable/remove steps; where possible, use ephemeral or manually invoked mechanisms instead of persistent automatic hooks.","code_snippet":"\n### Option 1: Project-Level Configuration\n\nCreate `.claude/settings.json` in your project root:\n\n```json\n{","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c21e27d263e380f761137d8f8d1a607f60990e76d123b08eced99ad5b73b4972","occurrences":[{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":15,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-8098ee47ff9640d085eba3a47a9eb116","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"An empty matcher causes the UserPromptSubmit hook to trigger on every prompt, creating an always-on execution path. In an agent environment, broad automatic triggering increases attack surface, raises the chance of prompt-driven abuse or unexpected side effects, and makes it harder for users to reason about when code will run.","remediation":"Replace the empty matcher with a narrowly scoped pattern tied to specific workflows, or disable automatic triggering by default and require explicit opt-in. Document the trigger conditions clearly and provide least-privilege examples.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-f54774e36ff847dea4325573895617ec","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":48,"end_line":55},"finding":null,"explanation":"This guidance combines two risky properties: user-level installation in ~/.claude/settings.json and an empty matcher that activates on all prompts globally. That creates persistent, broad-scope command execution across sessions and repositories, so any bug or malicious modification in the hooked script can affect all future agent use.","remediation":"Do not recommend global activation with an empty matcher. Prefer project-local configuration, require explicit scoping, and warn users that user-level hooks persist across all sessions; additionally, use absolute trusted paths, integrity checks, and clear uninstall instructions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":48,"end_line":55}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-4b29e94affaa4a0c9aa17b079e7a6f2d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":70,"end_line":77},"finding":null,"explanation":"Although labeled 'minimal,' this setup still uses an empty matcher, so the hook executes for every prompt rather than only for relevant self-improvement events. That broad trigger scope can cause unnecessary code execution, information exposure through hook context, and unanticipated behavior in unrelated tasks.","remediation":"Make the minimal example actually minimal in scope by using a restrictive matcher or a manual invocation mechanism. Explain the tradeoff between convenience and exposure, and default to the safer narrower configuration.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":70,"end_line":77}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-d21d432c271442bf897efce9eb3e2cd8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":92,"end_line":99},"finding":null,"explanation":"The Codex CLI example repeats the empty matcher pattern, enabling the command hook for every prompt. In a coding-agent workflow, that means pervasive automatic script execution, which amplifies the consequences of script compromise, prompt abuse, or simple implementation mistakes.","remediation":"Provide a scoped matcher for Codex as well, or recommend disabled-by-default hooks with explicit enablement for debugging or learning-capture sessions. Add warnings about reviewing and pinning the referenced script before installation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":92,"end_line":99}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-f33410d9ecc3417db4b3e4957e3ba1cf","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":205,"end_line":207},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document claims the hook scripts 'only output text' and 'don't modify files or run commands,' but the configuration explicitly installs them as command hooks and even shows invoking another shell script. This misleading assurance can cause operators to grant trust or permissions they would not otherwise allow, increasing the chance of unsafe execution in a high-trust agent context.","remediation":"Correct the security section to accurately state that these are executable command hooks that run with the agent's permissions. Document the exact trust boundary, expected side effects, and required code review of each script; if possible, replace shell hooks with safer declarative mechanisms or restrict execution to audited, read-only scripts.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/hooks-setup.md","start_line":205,"end_line":207}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-e23e6c1142054e1fac862071224fcc70","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"references/openclaw-integration.md","start_line":57,"end_line":null},"finding":"Create Learning Files\n\nCreate the `.learnings/` directory in your workspace:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.openclaw/workspace/.learnings\n```\n\nOr in the skill directory:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.openclaw","explanation":"The integration explicitly creates a persistent `.learnings/` directory, enabling session-derived information to survive resets and be reused later. In a self-improvement skill, that persistence materially increases the chance that sensitive user content, operational details, or incorrect guidance become durable state and influence future behavior beyond the original session.","remediation":"Minimize what is stored, default to ephemeral or user-approved persistence, and add retention, review, and deletion controls for `.learnings/`. Clearly separate project-specific notes from global memory and require explicit confirmation before writing potentially sensitive or cross-session data.","code_snippet":"openclaw hooks enable self-improvement\n```\n\n### 3. Create Learning Files\n\nCreate the `.learnings/` directory in your workspace:\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3fcf971141a3cc9de9e85413d694fbfcf3bb026a1edcf998f758d5b6dc7afeb6","occurrences":[{"file":"references/openclaw-integration.md","start_line":57,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-03c091a34f6e460d881981e8051ccf80","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/openclaw-integration.md","start_line":199,"end_line":205},"finding":null,"explanation":"The 'Detection Triggers' section lists generic conditions such as 'Knowledge gaps', 'API errors', and user corrections like 'No, that's wrong...' without clearly constraining when the skill should activate or when it should not. These phrases overlap with common interaction patterns and lack negative examples or scope boundaries, making unintended invocation more likely.","remediation":"Define a narrow, explicit set of activation conditions tied to specific OpenClaw events or commands, and include exclusion criteria or negative examples showing when these signals should not trigger the skill.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/openclaw-integration.md","start_line":199,"end_line":205}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-676bfaa6d372484391528a461e58675e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/openclaw-integration.md","start_line":57,"end_line":69},"finding":null,"explanation":"The setup instructions direct users to create persistent learning storage in workspace or skill directories without clearly warning that future runs may write durable data there. This can surprise users, lead to retention of sensitive prompts or errors, and increase privacy risk in environments where workspace contents are synced or shared.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning before setup that the skill persists learnings to disk, describe what kinds of data may be stored, and recommend reviewing, redacting, or disabling persistence in sensitive environments. Provide configuration options for storage location, retention limits, and opt-in/opt-out behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/openclaw-integration.md","start_line":57,"end_line":69}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":785,"completion_tokens":217,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1002},{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":849,"completion_tokens":201,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1050},{"n